        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b2707d09-2fb3-5690-9f91-138998d868cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Operation Buster–Jangle\n- Places: Nevada Test Site, Nevada National Security Site, Nye County, Las Vegas\n- Organizations: United States, United States Department of Energy\n\nFacts:\n- In late 1951, Operation Buster–Jangle was a series of seven United States nuclear weapons tests.\n- Operation Buster–Jangle included six atmospheric tests and one cratering test.\n- Operation Buster–Jangle was conducted at the Nevada Test Site.\n- The Nevada National Security Site was previously called the Nevada Test Site.\n- The Nevada National Security Site is a United States Department of Energy reservation.\n- The Nevada National Security Site is in southeastern Nye County, Nevada, about 65 miles northwest of Las Vegas.",
